{
  "description": "The PICO agent's num_ctx and stop, Python and Rust alike (#640, #641, #642). Each case runs the real agent, the real map-reduce and a real client over a fake Ollama HTTP transport (Python: ollama-python over an httpx.MockTransport). A JSON-mode request is answered with `json_reply` (it reads as both a suitability check and an extraction), a plain one with `digest`. `text` is `text_unit` repeated `text_repeat` times. With `stop_at_request` k (0-based) the stop is set as request k arrives, and that request then fails (`request_at_stop: fails`, a transport fault) or answers. `stop_before` sets it before the run. Each k in `fail_requests` fails request k with a transport fault and no stop, which the condenser's model retries up to `context_model_attempts` tries; `malformed_request` k answers request k with a body that is not JSON, which is not retried, and `malformed_from_request` k answers request k and every later one so. `status_request` k answers request k with HTTP `status` (body `{\"error\": \"refused\"}`), and `status_from_request` k answers request k and every later one so: a status in `retried_statuses` is retried, any other is not (#646). `expected.requests` is how many requests reached the transport, every one carrying the case's `num_ctx` (the key absent when null); `expected.error` is the error kind, or null for a result; a `request_failed` states `expected.retryable`, whether a retry may cure it (#659: a transport fault or a status in `retried_statuses`), and no other case does; it states `expected.status` too, the HTTP status the server answered with, or null where none came or the answer was unreadable (#662). `fn: prepare` is `prepare` alone; `fn: prepared` is `prepare`, then `check_suitability_prepared` and `extract_prepared`; at this budget a 60-unit text takes four condensation requests (four batches whose digests fit merged). `expected.note` is null when the result carries no note, else substrings its one note contains: the status and the failed batch's cause (#658). A long paper whose every condensation batch fails is `request_failed` as a short paper's failed request is, with the `retryable` and `status` of its worst failed request: one no retry cures over one a retry may, and among equals the last (#616). `expected.progress` is every report the condenser's progress callback received, in order, each written `\"<stage> <current_batch>/<total_batches> level <recursion_level> items <current_item>/<total_items>\"`; a text that needs no condensation reports none (#609). The condensed text is one item split across the batches, which counts once, when its last piece's batch is done, never 3 of 1 (#673).",
  "stopped_kind": "stopped",
  "model": "ollama:test-model",
  "title": "A trial",
  "text_unit": "Adults aged 40-65 were randomised to metformin or placebo. ",
  "digest": "Adults aged 40-65 were randomised to metformin or placebo.",
  "min_similarity": 0.9,
  "max_context_chars": 1000,
  "context_model_attempts": 3,
  "retried_statuses": [408, 429, 500, 502, 503, 504, 529],
  "json_reply": {
    "is_intervention_study": true,
    "has_comparison": true,
    "is_suitable": true,
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "rationale": "An RCT of metformin against placebo.",
    "study_type": "randomized controlled trial",
    "sample_size": "N=120",
    "population": {"description": "Adults aged 40 to 65", "reported": true, "confidence": 0.9, "quotes": ["Adults aged 40-65"]},
    "intervention": {"description": "Metformin", "reported": true, "confidence": 0.9, "quotes": ["metformin"]},
    "comparison": {"description": "Placebo", "reported": true, "confidence": 0.9, "quotes": ["placebo"]},
    "outcome": {"description": "Not stated", "reported": false, "confidence": 0.5, "quotes": []}
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "a whole paper's extraction carries num_ctx",
      "fn": "extract", "num_ctx": 8192, "text_repeat": 1,
      "expected": {"requests": 1, "error": null, "note": null,
        "progress": []}
    },
    {
      "name": "no num_ctx sends none",
      "fn": "extract", "num_ctx": null, "text_repeat": 1,
      "expected": {"requests": 1, "error": null, "note": null,
        "progress": []}
    },
    {
